    </ul>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <!-- Hero (swap background image in CSS) -->
    <section class="hero" aria-label="Commissioned shoots hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <p class="kicker">Commissioned Shoots</p>
        <h1>Understated. Editorial. Finished.</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          A commissioned shoot is not a quick photo session. It’s a tailored, editorial-style experience designed to create finished images—clean, intentional, and built to hold up on a large screen, in print, or in a feature story.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-meta">
          <span class="pill">Limited commissions</span>
          <span class="pill">Curated delivery</span>
          <span class="pill">Santa Clara, Utah</span>
          <span class="pill">Available nationwide</span>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn" href="#request">Request a Commission</a>
          <a class="btn secondary" href="/about.html">About Thomas</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <p class="muted" style="margin:0; max-width:78ch;">
        I take on a limited number of commissions so each project gets full attention from planning through final delivery.
        If you’re looking for images that feel like they belong in a magazine—this is for you.
      </p>

      <div class="rule"></div>

      <h2>What you can expect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Consultation first</strong> to align on the look, location, and how you’ll use the images</li>
        <li><strong>Guidance and direction</strong> during the shoot (posing the car, angles, lighting, pacing)</li>
        <li><strong>A curated set of fully edited final images</strong>—not a dump of hundreds of files</li>
        <li><strong>Consistent color and retouching</strong> with a premium, natural finish</li>
        <li><strong>Professional delivery</strong> in high-resolution + web-ready formats</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section>
      <h2>Commission Options</h2>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Local Commission</h3>
          <div class="price">$500 <span>— a tight, curated session</span></div>
          <p class="tagline">
            For local owners who want finished images without turning it into a full production.
          </p>

          <div class="rule"></div>

          <p class="muted"><strong>Includes:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Quick consult to plan location and style</li>
            <li>Up to <strong>60 minutes</strong> of shooting within <strong>30 minutes of Santa Clara, Utah</strong></li>
            <li>A curated gallery of <strong>fully edited final images</strong> delivered ready to share or print</li>
            <li>Optional upgrades available (including <strong>gallery-quality metal prints</strong> by request)</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="bestfor"><strong>Best for:</strong> personal keepsakes, social content, tasteful marketplace listings, gifts.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Signature Commission</h3>
          <p class="tagline">
            Expanded planning and coverage—designed to create a fuller set of images with more variety, intention, and story.
          </p>

          <div class="rule"></div>

          <p class="muted"><strong>Designed to include:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Pre-shoot planning (locations, timing, visual direction)</li>
            <li>Extended shoot time and optional multi-location coverage</li>
            <li>A larger curated set of finals with deeper retouching consistency</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="bestfor"><strong>Best for:</strong> cars with provenance, full builds, collector cars, sponsor decks, brand content.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Editorial Feature Commission</h3>
          <p class="tagline">
            Planned like a feature and executed with the same care—built around the car, the setting, and the story it deserves.
          </p>

          <div class="rule"></div>

          <p class="muted"><strong>Designed to include:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Travel planning and scheduling in blocks</li>
            <li>Multi-location coverage for a complete story arc</li>
            <li>A fully curated, magazine-ready delivery set</li>
            <li>Optional written feature article to document or memorialize the car and its story</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="muted2" style="margin:.8rem 0 0;"><strong>Note:</strong> Travel and accommodations are scoped per project.</p>
          <p class="bestfor"><strong>Best for:</strong> historically significant race cars, high-end builds, rare collectors, brand building, and cars with a sentimental story worth documenting properly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section class="panel">
      <h2>Owner Prep Guide</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:.25rem 0 0; max-width:78ch;">
        You don’t need to overthink this—but a little prep makes a big difference in the final images.
      </p>

      <div class="rule"></div>

      <h3>Detail matters</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Full detail recommended (paint, wheels, glass, interior). Same-day detail is ideal.</li>
        <li>Clean tires/wheels are the fastest way to make a car look expensive in photos.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rule"></div>

      <h3>Bring a quick touch-up kit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Window cleaner + microfiber (glass shows everything)</li>
        <li>Soft duster or clean microfiber for light dust</li>
        <li>Optional: a light tire dressing (use sparingly—best applied after the car is positioned)</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rule"></div>

      <h3>Keep the car “photo-ready”</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Remove parking passes, cables, clutter, and anything in cup holders</li>
        <li>If we’re shooting interior, wipe screens and the gauge cluster</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rule"></div>

      <h3>Lights without idling</h3>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:.25rem 0 0; max-width:80ch;">
        Headlights and interior lighting can add a unique look—especially during golden hour. A <strong>strong battery</strong> helps so we can keep the engine <strong>off</strong>.
        Idling can create subtle vibrations that reduce sharpness—especially in close-ups and interior shots.
      </p>

      <div class="rule"></div>

      <h3>Timing makes the look</h3>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:.25rem 0 0; max-width:80ch;">
        Golden hour (sunrise/sunset) is the most flattering light. Midday is workable, but it’s harsher and less forgiving.
      </p>

      <div class="rule"></div>

      <h3>Weather and flexibility</h3>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:.25rem 0 0; max-width:80ch;">
        If weather doesn’t cooperate, we’ll adjust timing or reschedule—no stress.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section id="request" class="cta" aria-label="Request a commission">
      <div>
        <strong>Request a Commission</strong>
        <p>
          Tell me what you’re driving, what you want the images to feel like, and where you’re located.
          I’ll recommend the best option and confirm scope before booking.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-actions" style="margin:0;">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact.html?subject=Commissioned%20Shoot%20Inquiry">Start a Request</a>
        <a class="btn secondary" href="/prints.html">Explore Prints</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div>© <span id="year"></span> Thomas LeClair Photography</div>
    <div class="footlinks">
      <a href="/index.html">Home</a>
      <a href="/about.html">About</a>
      <a href="/contact.html">Contact</a>
      <a href="/prints.html">Prints</a>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    // Footer year
    document.getElementById("year").textContent = new Date().getFullYear();

    // Auto-hide nav: show when scrolling up, hide when scrolling down
    const nav = document.getElementById("siteNav");
    let lastY = window.scrollY;
    let ticking = false;

    function onScroll(){
      const y = window.scrollY;
      const goingUp = y < lastY;

      if (y < 40) nav.classList.remove("show");
      else nav.classList.toggle("show", goingUp);

      lastY = y;
      ticking = false;
    }

    window.addEventListener("scroll", () => {
      if (!ticking){
        window.requestAnimationFrame(onScroll);
        ticking = true;
      }
    });

    // Show nav briefly on load (subtle)
    window.addEventListener("load", () => {
      setTimeout(() => nav.classList.add("show"), 120);
      setTimeout(() => nav.classList.remove("show"), 1200);
    });
  </script>
</body>
